WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.863 --> 00:00:21.750
Before you start: disposable MSP SLA policy for White Rabbit (SLA settings)

2
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:27.747
1. Configure and persist the customer-to-MSP priority mapping

3
00:00:27.747 --> 00:00:39.932
2. Escalation starts the MSP obligation (not initial visibility)

4
00:00:39.932 --> 00:00:53.999
3. Change the mapping: existing targets stay, new escalation uses current config

5
00:00:53.999 --> 00:00:59.524
5 (prep). MSP assigns ticket 2 to QA so threshold notices have an assignee

6
00:00:59.524 --> 00:01:10.685
4. MSP returns ticket 1 to the customer; history preserved

7
00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:23.155
5. Departed relationship: Kansas Farms keeps its own outcome; MSP live read unavailable

8
00:01:23.155 --> 00:08:01.857
5. Breach/routing notification on ticket 2 (4-minute response target)

9
00:08:01.857 --> 00:08:13.270
Restore: mapping back to original, policy unassigned from White Rabbit
